# Symbols allowed in .bss/.data of the embedded firmware.
#
# The rule is ZERO framework statics, not "a small number of bytes".
# `docs/results-embedded.md` budgeted `.bss + .data <= 2 KB` until
# 2026-09-07, and that threshold was never approached — a bound nothing
# has come near tells you nothing. What the number was really asserting
# is a *shape*: that this framework has no hidden global state. No
# allocator arena, no lazily-initialised registry, no static caches,
# nothing that claims RAM before `main`.
#
# So the check is zero, and anything genuinely needed is named here with
# a reason. A framework symbol appearing in this file should be an
# argument, not a formality.
#
# Format: one symbol name per line, `#` comments. Sizes are not listed:
# the point is which symbols exist, and a symbol that grows is still the
# same decision.

# --- the fixture's own harness, not the framework ---
# Where firmware.rs parks the frame checksum so the frame is not dead
# code. It is `#[no_mangle] pub` deliberately: as a private static it
# had no symbol at all, LLVM having removed the store, and the frame
# survived only on panic paths — true by accident. See its doc comment.
SINK
